♪ (crowd) Version it, or clone and own. ♪

213
00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:25.340
♪ pytest runs the tests you wrote: library or framework? ♪

214
00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:28.733
♪ (crowd) Framework: it calls your code. ♪

215
00:12:29.033 --> 00:12:34.221
(narrator) The final chorus completes the hall's belfries and roofs and the building site's upper wall courses.

216
00:12:34.221 --> 00:12:37.645
(narrator) Each question appears in turn beside the growing gold brick tower.

217
00:12:37.645 --> 00:12:45.375
(narrator) Case tags connect each question to its example: Ariane 5 for assumptions, left-pad for dependencies, urllib3 and Heartbleed for pinning and updating.

218
00:12:45.375 --> 00:12:48.384
(narrator) The final takeaway lights, and paper confetti drifts down.

219
00:12:48.987 --> 00:12:50.847
♪ Before you reuse, ask: ♪

220
00:12:50.847 --> 00:12:53.147
♪ What will it save? What will it cost? ♪

221
00:12:53.147 --> 00:12:54.987
♪ What does it assume? ♪

222
00:12:54.987 --> 00:12:57.387
♪ What does it pull in? ♪

223
00:12:58.127 --> 00:12:59.927
♪ Pin it, but update for patches. ♪

224
00:12:59.927 --> 00:13:05.667
♪ External reuse is not a one-time investment. ♪

225
00:13:06.867 --> 00:13:12.882
(narrator) The outro: your hero steps forward on the brick site, singing beside a terminal that shows npm install left-pad.

226
00:13:12.882 --> 00:13:16.695
(narrator) A JavaScript example replaces the terminal: String of str dot padStart.

227
00:13:16.695 --> 00:13:18.467
(narrator) Eleven lines become one built-in.

228
00:13:18.467 --> 00:13:26.093
(narrator) Directly over the site, five case bricks stack into one build: reuse done right, and the foreman, carrying a gold brick, gives it a thumbs-up.

229
00:13:26.093 --> 00:13:29.530
(narrator) Behind it, the crane sets its prebuilt module onto the building.

230
00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.108
(narrator) The sun has risen to the right into golden hour.

231
00:13:32.108 --> 00:13:37.532
(narrator) The upper sky is bright blue, the horizon glows gold, and the clouds have peach and cream undersides.

232
00:13:37.532 --> 00:13:39.466
(narrator) The stars and site lamps have faded.

233
00:13:39.466 --> 00:13:42.419
(narrator) The completed composition holds through the final note.

234
00:13:43.013 --> 00:13:45.613
npm install left-pad?

235
00:13:45.613 --> 00:13:50.113
No need: padStart is built in.

236
00:13:50.703 --> 00:13:53.553
That's reuse done right.

237
00:13:53.553 --> 00:14:00.700
[music]
